
# Beads / Dolt files (added by bd init)
.dolt/
*.db
.beads-credential-key

# Claude Code agent worktrees (ephemeral, per-agent isolated copies)
.claude/worktrees/

# Python bytecode cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Rust / Cargo build artifacts (yf workspace)
/target/

# Skill runtime state + local config (never committed; per Skill Surface Convention)
/.yf/
# ...with ONE carve-out (REQ-YF-PRE-004a): the COMMITTED shared config tier
# `.yf/<short>/config.json`. Everything else under /.yf/ — all runtime state and
# every *.local.json — stays ignored. Git will not descend into an ignored
# directory, so the two `!` directory lines are required before the file rule.
!/.yf/
!/.yf/*/
/.yf/*/*
!/.yf/*/config.json
/.yf-plan.local.json
/.yf-research.local.json
/.agent-shell/

/.worktrees/

# Skill runtime state + local config (bdplan; Surface Convention §6)
/.bdplan.local.json
/.state/

# Skill runtime state + local config (yf-beads-init; Surface Convention §6)
/.yf-beads-init.local.json

# Skill runtime state + local config (yf-plan; Surface Convention §6)
/.beads/formulas/

# beads-init: required exclusions
.beads/proxieddb/

# yf-okf-hygiene scaffolding (plan-064 Issue 1.7 / #294).
#
# These two directories are created by `okf_hygiene.py backfill` INSIDE the bundle roots — and
# `docs/plans/*` is a depth-1 glob that matches them, because `pathlib.Path.glob('*')` matches
# dot-prefixed names (unlike `glob.glob`). `Journal.clear()`'s own docstring records that this
# already cost a `64 -> 66` inflation of the enumerated bundle count.
#
# They SURVIVE A HALT by design (that is what makes crash recovery possible), so they are not
# transient enough to ignore in practice, and they were untracked-but-NOT-ignored — precisely
# the class the corrected REQ-OKF-CHK-004 predicate keeps ENUMERATED. Ignoring them is the
# right remedy: they are genuinely not members, and the driver's root filter cannot see them
# because it filters bundle ROOTS, one level above where they sit.
#
# NO TRAILING SLASH, deliberately. A `dir/` pattern is DIRECTORY-ONLY, and git can only apply
# that when the path exists on disk — so `git check-ignore docs/plans/.okf-hygiene-staging`
# returns 1 (not ignored) whenever the scaffolding is absent, which is most of the time and is
# exactly when a criterion would be checking it. The bare-name form matches regardless.
.okf-hygiene-staging
.okf-hygiene-journal
